{
  "id": "lesson-redux-001",
  "slug": "what-is-redux",
  "moduleSlug": "redux-fundamentals",
  "title": "What is Redux",
  "description": "Understand Redux and its place in React applications.",
  "order": 1,
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedMinutes": 18,
  "tags": ["redux", "state", "management", "introduction"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Redux** is a predictable state container for JavaScript applications. It helps you write applications that behave consistently and are easy to test."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Why Redux?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Predictable**: State changes follow strict rules",
          "**Centralized**: All state in one place",
          "**Debuggable**: Time-travel debugging with DevTools",
          "**Flexible**: Works with any UI layer",
          "**Maintainable**: Clear separation of concerns"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "When to Use Redux"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Large amounts of application state",
          "State updated frequently",
          "Complex state update logic",
          "Large codebase with many developers",
          "Need for time-travel debugging"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Redux Data Flow"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Redux follows a unidirectional data flow: **View → Action → Reducer → Store → View**"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "data": {
        "variant": "info",
        "title": "Modern Redux",
        "text": "Modern Redux uses Redux Toolkit, which simplifies most Redux tasks and is the recommended approach."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "summary-box",
      "data": {
        "title": "Key Takeaways",
        "points": [
          "Redux is a predictable state container",
          "Follows unidirectional data flow",
          "Useful for complex state management",
          "Redux Toolkit is the modern approach"
        ],
        "takeaway": "Redux provides predictable state management for complex apps."
      }
    }
  ],
